// Adjacent to 0904: the same past-anchor `since` divergence, but the left side
// correlates on TWO current-request keys (`input.user` AND `input.region`).
//
// This guards against a fix that threads only ONE correlation column through
// the since-anchor branch of the §5.3 rewrite: a one-column fix would still
// drop `region`, so the outer identity join would fail on the second key and
// the verdict would (still wrongly) be false. Both keys must be carried.
//
// The interpreter is the oracle (see expected_1.out); DSQL is a known
// verdict divergence until the temporal-compiler since-left correlation fix
// lands. Found by the SMT differential fuzzer.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{
        input.user: context.input.user,
        input.region: context.input.region
     }
        && context.input.amount >= 10)
    since within 1h
    Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: "carol" }
};
